# What the exhaustive run costs: one pass, eight stages, and the counts that
# pass printed. Windows 11 10.0.26300, RTX 3060, warm build directories
# (every template had been built already), 2026-11-28.
#
# One pass, in this order. Each stage was stopped on its own with
# `date +%s%N` around it, and one stopwatch ran from the first stage to the
# last, so the rows and the total describe the same sitting - the earlier file
# evidence/2026-11-27-windows/suite-timings.log holds four passes whose rows
# were sometimes separated by a minute of orchestration; this one does not.
#
# The counts are the ones this pass printed, which is why the CUDA row is now
# the 584-check suite (162 x 3 + 98, the gpux run included) and not the 486 of
# the 2026-11-27 reading. That pass read 127.3 s on its stopwatch; this one reads
# 124.2 s, and the difference is the machine's load, not the 98 extra checks.
#
